<div class="paper-block-grid">
  <div class="paper-summary">
    <div class="paper-badge mono">
      <span>Accepted · ICSSIT 2026 · Paper ID 1849</span>
    </div>
    <h3 class="paper-title">
      Probabilistic Space Debris Conjunction Assessment Using Machine Learning and Covariance Intersection Analysis
    </h3>
    <p class="paper-authors">
      <em>Fenil Miteshkumar Modi</em>, Satvik V. Khara, Gaurav D. Tivari, Jay Patel, Prathmesh Patel, Gautam Kumawat
    </p>
    <p class="paper-venue">
      Department of Computer Engineering, Silver Oak University · Technically sponsored by the IEEE SMC Society
    </p>
    <div class="paper-actions">
      <a href="/research" class="btn btn-pri">Read Research Paper</a>
      <a href="/projects/orcas" class="btn">View ORCAS System</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <aside class="paper-result">
    <div class="pr-head mono">
      <span>Validation · T₀ 2009-02-10 16:56 UTC</span>
      <h4>Iridium 33 / Cosmos 2251</h4>
    </div>

    <dl class="pr-rows mono">
      <div><dt>Altitude</dt><dd>788.6 km</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Relative velocity</dt><dd>7.46 / 7.42 km s⁻¹</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Covariance det. (P)</dt><dd>2.4 × 10⁴ km²</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Covariance det. (S)</dt><dd>4.1 × 10⁴ km²</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Mahalanobis <i>D<sub>M</sub></i></dt><dd>1.84</dd></div>
      <div class="hi"><dt>Probability <i>P<sub>c</sub></i></dt><dd>4.2 × 10⁻³</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Alert threshold</dt><dd>1.0 × 10⁻⁴</dd></div>
    </dl>

    <p class="pr-verdict">
      Two orders of magnitude above threshold. Deterministic models called this a <b>miss</b>. The probabilistic pipeline flags it <span class="crit mono">CRITICAL</span>.
    </p>
  </aside>
</div>

